# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — .gitignore
# Stack-agnostic baseline. Add stack-specific ignores once gspec/stack.md is set
# (the gspec `stack` skill decides the stack).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Environment / secrets — never commit credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Orchestration run-state — local guided-loop session bookkeeping, not product
# history. Gitignored so the single-checkout discard (`git stash -u`) and
# `git add -A` never sweep or commit it, and so it never dirties the tree that
# `runstate.sh reconcile` inspects (ADR 0009). Persists on local disk.
.agents/run-state.yaml

# The two files that TRAVEL WITH run-state and must share its treatment exactly
# (plugin ADR 0022, ADR 0019 v3.4): the finding BODIES whose one-line index lives
# inside run-state, and the archived overflow of run-state's `note:`. Both are the
# cold half of a hot/cold split whose hot half is gitignored — so ignoring them is
# what keeps the pair consistent. Ignoring is also what makes them SURVIVE: an
# untracked file is swept by the pause path's `git stash --include-untracked` and
# shows up in the `git status --porcelain` that `reconcile` reads as scratch sitting
# on the green checkpoint (which it then discards). An ignored file is invisible to
# both, exactly like run-state.yaml.
.agents/findings/
.agents/run-state-note-archive.md

# The last-known-good copy `runstate.sh write` takes before replacing run-state.
# It exists because run-state is gitignored: a botched upstream transform in a pipe
# destroyed it permanently, with no `git restore` to fall back on. It MUST be
# ignored for the reason the block above spells out — an untracked file is swept by
# the pause path's stash and discarded by reconcile as scratch, so an unignored
# backup would be destroyed by the very recovery path it exists to serve.
.agents/run-state-prev.yaml

# Orchestration run-metrics — the event spine + assembled per-run metrics packets
# (plugin ADR 0019 Tier 1). Local run bookkeeping, NOT product history; gitignored
# for the same ADR 0009 reasons as run-state above. The assembled run-metrics.json
# is a portable single file — archive a run by copying it out, not by committing
# this live directory. The bare-prefix glob also covers an archived copy named
# `.agents/metrics-<id>/`.
.agents/metrics/
.agents/metrics*

# Orchestration pause sentinel(s) — the cooperative-pause REQUEST channel (ADR
# 0017). Transient, machine-local, and NOT product history: a running loop/lanes
# poll `.agents/pause` (all) or `.agents/pause.<task-id>` (one lane) at safe
# checkpoints and wrap up to a green commit. Gitignored so a request never dirties
# a lane's tree or gets committed.
.agents/pause
.agents/pause.*

# OS-generated files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editors / IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*~

# Common build / dependency output (harmless if unused)
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
target/
bin/
obj/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
coverage/
